WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:02.420
- I mean you can't call
that a baguette, really,

00:00:02.420 --> 00:00:04.880
or you would be jailed in France.

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:08.590
(playful guitar strumming)

00:00:08.590 --> 00:00:09.740
My name is Gus Reckel.

00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:11.730
I'm the owner of L'imprimerie.

00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:13.600
Being French, I've been
baking my entire life.

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:16.110
Today, we're gonna taste some
free bread from restaurants

00:00:16.110 --> 00:00:16.943
all over America.

00:00:16.943 --> 00:00:18.461
I'm very excited.

00:00:18.461 --> 00:00:23.160
(lightly playful accordion music)

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:24.065
It's really light.

00:00:24.065 --> 00:00:26.225
Soft, smooth, pillowy, that's good.

00:00:26.225 --> 00:00:27.058
(sniffing)

00:00:27.058 --> 00:00:27.960
It smells like buttery.

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:30.120
It's very, very, very dense.

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:31.280
It's almost briochey.

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:32.305
Did you bring cheese?

00:00:32.305 --> 00:00:33.138
You did?

00:00:33.138 --> 00:00:34.470
You didn't, no cheese.

00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:36.555
No cheese, no butter.

00:00:36.555 --> 00:00:37.388
Mmm.

00:00:37.388 --> 00:00:38.221
It's not bad.

00:00:38.221 --> 00:00:39.054
The flavor is good.

00:00:39.054 --> 00:00:40.530
Texture from the outside is very nice,

00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:42.410
and then it becomes
like almost too fluffy.

00:00:42.410 --> 00:00:43.243
Very doughy.

00:00:43.243 --> 00:00:45.676
We give like maybe two
stars to start with.

00:00:45.676 --> 00:00:50.230
(lightly playful accordion music)

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:51.063
Red Lobster.

00:00:51.063 --> 00:00:53.120
Beyonce called it in a
song, so it should be good.

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:53.953
It's very oily.

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:54.840
The cheese, I guess.

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:56.547
The biscuit is very dense.

00:00:56.547 --> 00:00:57.380
(sniffing)

00:00:57.380 --> 00:00:59.040
It smells like (sniffing)

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:01.513
there is like butter and herbs.

00:01:02.530 --> 00:01:03.363
Mmm, um.

00:01:03.363 --> 00:01:04.210
It's not very cheesy.

00:01:04.210 --> 00:01:05.080
I think they look good.

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:06.400
On the shelf, I would pick one up.

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:07.233
Well, not this one.

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:08.380
But the other one was good.

00:01:08.380 --> 00:01:13.222
Three stars because it's
free and cheesy and greasy?

00:01:13.222 --> 00:01:17.460
(lightly playful accordion music)

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:18.510
It's very pillowy,

00:01:18.510 --> 00:01:20.040
in a good way, but no crunch.

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:22.062
If you push it, it becomes mushy.

00:01:22.062 --> 00:01:23.280
(sniffing)

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:24.540
It doesn't smell like anything really.

00:01:24.540 --> 00:01:25.590
It does smell like warm bread.

00:01:25.590 --> 00:01:26.620
Warm bread is always good.

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:27.453
Can take the rolls, whatever,

00:01:27.453 --> 00:01:28.700
when it's warm, it's good.

00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:30.280
Mmm, this is very sweet.

00:01:30.280 --> 00:01:33.729
This is like sugar, or maybe
a bit of honey, or molasses.

00:01:33.729 --> 00:01:34.562
It is so sweet.

00:01:34.562 --> 00:01:35.395
It is pure sugar.

00:01:35.395 --> 00:01:36.228
There goes my beach body.

00:01:36.228 --> 00:01:37.061
Here comes the dad bod.

00:01:37.061 --> 00:01:37.894
The flavor is okay.

00:01:37.894 --> 00:01:38.800
More like a brioche.

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:40.980
I think, three stars for the effort.

00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:42.680
It comes with butter to make it better.

00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:44.848
Everything is better with butter.

00:01:44.848 --> 00:01:49.015
(lightly playful accordion music)

00:01:50.088 --> 00:01:50.921
Really soft.

00:01:50.921 --> 00:01:51.876
That's a good thing.

00:01:51.876 --> 00:01:52.780
That fact that it comes with the butter,

00:01:52.780 --> 00:01:54.325
makes it more interesting.

00:01:54.325 --> 00:01:55.158
(sniffing)

00:01:55.158 --> 00:01:55.991
No yeast.

00:01:55.991 --> 00:01:57.200
It's not unpleasant; now the inside.

00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:59.630
We back to this mushy, airy.

00:01:59.630 --> 00:02:01.640
Let's see how they taste.

00:02:01.640 --> 00:02:02.990
Mmm, this one is very sweet too.

00:02:02.990 --> 00:02:03.880
In a kind of good way,

00:02:03.880 --> 00:02:06.010
but not in a way I was expecting.

00:02:06.010 --> 00:02:07.410
This is a spread.

00:02:07.410 --> 00:02:08.780
Gonna makes it even sweeter.

00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:10.480
Yeah, no beach for me this summer.

00:02:12.521 --> 00:02:14.030
Mmm.

00:02:14.030 --> 00:02:14.863
It's not for me.

00:02:14.863 --> 00:02:18.169
I would give maybe one star.

00:02:18.169 --> 00:02:22.960
(lightly playful accordion music)

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:24.610
I think we're supposed
to have a brown one,

00:02:24.610 --> 00:02:26.940
but I guess it's so good
that it got eaten on the way.

00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:28.070
So we're going to try only this one.

00:02:28.070 --> 00:02:29.940
Close as it looks to French bread,

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:30.773
let's see.

00:02:30.773 --> 00:02:33.206
You could have a good surprise, maybe.

00:02:33.206 --> 00:02:34.039
(knocking)

00:02:34.039 --> 00:02:35.300
The sound is not too bad.

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:38.180
There's little fermentation
and little love.

00:02:38.180 --> 00:02:39.610
Maybe the brown one was better,

00:02:39.610 --> 00:02:40.796
but we don't have it, so.

00:02:40.796 --> 00:02:41.629
(crackling)

00:02:41.629 --> 00:02:42.462
Make some noise,

00:02:42.462 --> 00:02:45.209
but it's more the noise
of like, stale bread.

00:02:45.209 --> 00:02:46.450
It's very chewy and very hard.

00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:48.400
Not hard as in crispy, just hard as in,

00:02:50.490 --> 00:02:51.323
as in hard.

00:02:51.323 --> 00:02:52.270
The crumb is okay.

00:02:52.270 --> 00:02:54.570
Two stars because they
tried to do French bread,

00:02:54.570 --> 00:02:57.260
but with maybe little success.

00:02:57.260 --> 00:02:58.940
I like the idea that restaurants America

00:02:58.940 --> 00:02:59.773
give bread to people.

00:02:59.773 --> 00:03:01.607
I think what we would love to see is more

00:03:01.607 --> 00:03:03.450
artisan bread everywhere.

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:04.510
French people, you know?

00:03:04.510 --> 00:03:06.660
We're just sassy and
catty and (chuckling).

00:03:09.395 --> 00:03:13.562
(lightly playful accordion music)

